        verification storyAdmittedGapsGuardsDoD : Test { :>> id = "1acc7a82-c79f-45b9-b23d-a67b4446d517"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED (D0191, accepted on their words 'agreed. proceed' to the presented plan): guards 43 and 44, both WARNING tier per the guided profile, both unit-owned via the D0139(D) assert-constraint declaration so unadopted processes are not gated. GUARD 43 release-recorded (deploy unit): every v-prefixed tag has a Release item naming it whose recorded commit matches the tag's; FIRST RUN CAUGHT BOTH DEFECT SHAPES IT EXISTS FOR - v0.1.0 had NO Release item (backfilled as release010 with the commit read from the tag itself: recorded, not invented) and v0.2.0's tag sits at e2c812f, two housekeeping commits past its recorded 425145d (git rev-list counted; the warning STANDS - the Release item is claudeOpus5's authored fact and D0108 forbids a non-owner overwrite; theirs or the human's to reconcile). GUARD 44 enrollment-binding (actor-enrollment unit): a machine binding must resolve to a registered Person or a kind-carrying Actor - until now NOTHING validated .keel/actor and a bad name surfaced only when a downstream write refused; scans this machine's real binding (1, clean). The two satisfied UNDER-GUARDED entries left process-enforcement.toml in the same commit (no tombstones); constraint defs added to guard-constraints.sysml; imports added to both unit files; guards.md + CLAUDE.md count 42 -> 44 in the same commit (doc-sync). Deliberately NOT taken: distributedCollaboration and migration - visible in the same lens read, excluded from the plan the human accepted, still recorded admitted gaps."; }
        part storyAdmittedGapsGuardsDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "5af37a38-fc16-4cbc-bce0-a23d7980f26e"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "1d84acd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    }

