    part admittedGapsGuardsCloseOutGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "e3ad8c7c-f720-4a75-9c47-02e8755bd475"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "1d84acd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification admittedGapsGuardsRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "f2827afa-fd83-47a7-a0d2-ee7072b0b45e"; :>> title = "Sprint 395 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN under rcRecurrence: none new - the escape-mangling family appeared and was caught pre-execution by the review-before-run practice the standing rule prescribes. WELL: run-the-guard-before-recording turned the sprint from bookkeeping into detection - guard 43 found a missing authored fact and a tag/record skew that four releases of manual discipline had not. The two remaining admitted gaps (distributedCollaboration: the existing ownership guard needs only its unit declaration; migration: the census is a view, not a guard) are one Decision away and were deliberately left outside this sprint's accepted scope. Estimate 2 pts, delivered 2."; }
